WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.063
Unit 3 is universal tenant restrictions.

2
00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:07.686
The tenant restrictions version two
policy comes first: default block,

3
00:00:07.686 --> 00:00:13.094
with partner policies for the agency's own
other tenants and each approved partner,

4
00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:15.837
as Access and Privilege,
appendix C, sets it.

5
00:00:15.837 --> 00:00:21.059
Then tagging applies that policy to devices
with the client, or on a remote network,

6
00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:23.593
without a proxy, so users can sign in only

7
00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:26.588
to tenants and applications
the policy allows.

8
00:00:26.588 --> 00:00:31.537
Know its reach: it covers the authentication
plane and the Microsoft Graph data

9
00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:34.612
plane, not the SharePoint
or Exchange data planes,

10
00:00:34.612 --> 00:00:37.237
which only device-side signaling reaches.

11
00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:42.299
The setting is tenant-wide, and the pages
the guide read show no report-only mode.

12
00:00:42.299 --> 00:00:45.975
So its pilot is the Microsoft
traffic profile's assignment,

13
00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:47.925
with the block query read daily.

14
00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:51.580
The rollback turns tagging
off; the policy stays.
